WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.300 --> 00:00:07.300
This is Learn Text.js, chapter
six: Data & Route Handlers.

2
00:00:08.220 --> 00:00:10.570
Acme Deploys needs real data.

3
00:00:10.620 --> 00:00:13.020
A page fetches it from its own origin,

4
00:00:13.060 --> 00:00:15.850
and a route handler in
the app folder answers.

5
00:00:15.900 --> 00:00:18.810
Handlers use the Web
Request and Response APIs,

6
00:00:18.860 --> 00:00:21.450
and they run on text dev and text start.

7
00:00:21.500 --> 00:00:24.540
Same origin, so no CORS.

8
00:00:26.140 --> 00:00:28.860
First, a route handler.

9
00:00:30.540 --> 00:00:33.130
Route handlers live next to your pages.

10
00:00:33.180 --> 00:00:38.970
Create app/api/deployments/route.ts.

11
00:00:39.020 --> 00:00:42.410
It imports the deployments,
and a helper that creates one.

12
00:00:42.460 --> 00:00:46.250
Export a function for each
HTTP method you handle.

13
00:00:46.300 --> 00:00:49.530
GET returns the list with Response.json.

14
00:00:49.580 --> 00:00:53.690
POST reads the JSON body of the
request and creates a deployment,

15
00:00:53.740 --> 00:00:56.860
then answers with status 201.

16
00:00:58.380 --> 00:01:02.170
While text dev is running, you can
call it from the console prompt.

17
00:01:02.220 --> 00:01:06.570
Fetch /api/deployments and await the JSON.

18
00:01:06.620 --> 00:01:08.730
The handler answers with an array.

19
00:01:08.780 --> 00:01:12.700
Expand it, and there's
one object per deployment.

20
00:01:15.220 --> 00:01:18.100
Next, fetch in a page.

21
00:01:19.620 --> 00:01:23.250
Now the deployments page asks
the handler for its rows.

22
00:01:23.300 --> 00:01:25.970
Swap the static import for React's hooks,

23
00:01:26.020 --> 00:01:29.250
Spinner and useInput,
and the Deployment type.

24
00:01:29.300 --> 00:01:32.210
Keep the rows and a loading flag in state.

25
00:01:32.260 --> 00:01:35.890
refetch sets loading, fetches
the list, and stores it.

26
00:01:35.940 --> 00:01:38.770
An effect runs it once,
when the page mounts.

27
00:01:38.820 --> 00:01:43.890
Press r to refetch, or n to post
a new deployment and then refetch.

28
00:01:43.940 --> 00:01:45.890
While loading, show a Spinner.

29
00:01:45.940 --> 00:01:49.540
Then render the rows,
each with its status.

30
00:01:51.060 --> 00:01:53.250
Here it is, on the lesson page.

31
00:01:53.300 --> 00:01:56.210
Click the pad first,
so the page has focus.

32
00:01:56.260 --> 00:02:00.370
Press r to refetch, and a spinner
shows while the data loads.

33
00:02:00.420 --> 00:02:03.010
To post a new deployment, press n.

34
00:02:03.060 --> 00:02:07.860
It shows up as building, and turns
ready once the build finishes.

35
00:02:10.380 --> 00:02:13.980
Last, loading and error states.

36
00:02:14.780 --> 00:02:20.250
Instead of tracking loading by hand,
add a loading.tsx next to the page.

37
00:02:20.300 --> 00:02:22.490
It's shown while the page suspends.

38
00:02:22.540 --> 00:02:27.050
An error.tsx next to it catches
anything the page throws.

39
00:02:27.100 --> 00:02:28.890
Both are plain components.

40
00:02:28.940 --> 00:02:31.580
This one returns the same Spinner.

41
00:02:33.300 --> 00:02:36.370
Handlers can also return a ReadableStream.

42
00:02:36.420 --> 00:02:40.610
This example from the docs sends
a server-sent event every second.

43
00:02:40.660 --> 00:02:44.530
It's how build logs stream into
the dashboard, line by line.

44
00:02:44.580 --> 00:02:49.060
The Route Handlers docs also
cover proxying a local daemon.

45
00:02:50.580 --> 00:02:51.650
Quick check.

46
00:02:51.700 --> 00:02:54.500
What do route handlers return?

47
00:02:55.820 --> 00:02:57.370
A Web Response.

48
00:02:57.420 --> 00:03:00.730
Handlers use the Web
Request and Response APIs,

49
00:03:00.780 --> 00:03:03.740
including ReadableStream for streaming.

50
00:03:04.860 --> 00:03:08.700
And which file is shown
while a route suspends?

51
00:03:10.020 --> 00:03:12.190
loading.tsx.

52
00:03:12.240 --> 00:03:18.480
It wraps the page in a Suspense
boundary, and error.tsx catches throws.

53
00:03:20.400 --> 00:03:25.550
Next, in chapter seven, you'll replace the
hand-rolled rows with a sortable Table,

54
00:03:25.600 --> 00:03:28.350
and add a chart that
never shifts the layout.

55
00:03:28.400 --> 00:03:30.000
See you there.
